@yegor256 There is nothing wrong with `FtRemote` class; it is indeed returning an empty body. The problem is that `RsPrint` prints both `head` and `body` to the output string:
```
    public void print(final OutputStream output) throws IOException {
        this.printHead(output);
        this.printBody(output);
    }
```
So the aforementioned test will never be true, because 
```
new JdkRequest(home)
.method("POST")
.body().set("returnsAnEmptyResponseBody").back()
.fetch().body()
```
from `TkEmpty()` will never return an empty String.

Is this he expected behavior of `RsPrint` or it should be fixed?

