@paulodamaso the problem is that when you use `TkEmpty` then you expect to receive empty body, but that's not the case. I think you are misunderstanding the client request from server response. The server response should be with empty body.

> .body().set("returnsAnEmptyResponseBody").back()

This line set's clients request, not server's response.

@t-izbassar Yes, it set the request to be sent to `TkEmpty()`, I was meant that. `TkEmpty` indeed sends the correct body (""), but it is changed in `RsPrint`, and this makes that we will never ever have an empty body in this case because we have header and body being sent in this request.

I don't think that it would be a wise thing to change this behavior because this class is used in `BkBase`, which is used in a lot of other back-end classes. Besides that I don't think that this behavior is wrong: after all the `HTTP` response is a just one big String with header and body tied one to another, so our `RsPrint` implementation shouldn't be different.

So I've changed the test so it does not fails anymore.

